      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T17:50:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure why this is here exactly. GetAxes happens here to get the axis parameters, not the current axis values. GetPalette is getting some palette\u0027s values, not really its parameters. It might make sense here to return the number of palettes available and the number of palette entries.\n\nThis function could return the number of available palettes, and GetPalette and resolvePaletteOverride should be merged to be more like computeAxisValues (maybe call it computePaletteValues to be parallel).",
      "revId": "88736c5aa3a705d561b690795ad8cb089f894daa",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d0fdabf4_6531677e",
        "filename": "src/ports/SkFontHost_FreeType.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 22
      },
      "lineNbr": 2054,
      "author": {
        "id": 6155
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T15:54:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I hope I understand your intention correctly. There\u0027s a chance I misunderstood the suggestion. Perhaps let me mostly respond to the second part first, then come to the first part of your comment. \n\n\u003e This function could return the number of available palettes, and GetPalette and resolvePaletteOverride should be merged to be more like computeAxisValues (maybe call it computePaletteValues to be parallel).\n\nI think, if I don\u0027t want to refactor the use of `scanFont` everywhere, the reason for the difference and two-step incantation of `scanFont` + `ResolvePaletteOverrides` is that only `scanFont` instantiations the temporary `FT_Face` to analyse the font blob and extract required information from the font.\n\nThat\u0027s what the similarity is between `GetAxes()` and `GetPalette()`, both are required as a sort of template to validate the `SkFontArguments` and fill those in / override them with user values.\n\nThe purpose is to have a fully resolved palette as a combination of what\u0027s in the font (extracted from `scanFont`), overridden with user `SkFontArguments::PaletteOverride` which needs to be stored in `SkFontData`. If `SkFontData` would not have a fully resolved palette, not all code path leading to `SkTypeface_FreeType::FaceRec::Make` and from there to `setupAxes(*data)` could set the correct palette.",
      "parentUuid": "93b9f90a_e444bcf6",
      "revId": "88736c5aa3a705d561b690795ad8cb089f894daa",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
